  {
   "approach": "Begin at the Pinkham Notch Visitor Center on Route 16 and hike up the Tuckerman Ravine Trail as far as the Hermit Lake Shelter. Over the bridge you reach the Sherburne Ski Trail; follow it uphill on the left fork to the foot of the Hillman's Highway slide path. Boott Spur Gully is the long gully on the left side of the rocky buttress that makes up Cathedral Gully's wall. Begin as for Hillman's Highway, then angle left through a brief band of spruce into the gully; the biggest ice bulge comes first, then long sections of snow. The lower slide paths see avalanche, ice and rockfall, so check the avalanche forecast.",
   "area_id": "nh_tuckerman_ravine",
   "descent": null,
   "descent_text": "The gully tops out at a col in the Boott Spur ridge. Skiers click in there; on foot, walk off by way of Hillman's Highway or the Glen Boulder Trail.",
   "description": null,
   "discipline": "ice",
   "grade": "WI2- Mod. Snow",
   "id": "nh_tuckerman_ravine_boott_spur_gully",
   "name": "Boott Spur Gully",
   "need_approach": false,
   "need_descent": true,
   "parent": "Mount Washington",
   "peak": "Tuckerman Ravine",
   "peak_elev": null,
   "peak_lat": 44.26177,
   "peak_lng": -71.29653,
   "pitches": 1
  },
  {
   "approach": "Begin at the Pinkham Notch Visitor Center on Route 16 and hike up the Tuckerman Ravine Trail as far as the Hermit Lake Shelter, with the whole ravine in view from there; the trail continues to the floor of the bowl. Climb Left Gully about halfway, then head left and bushwhack for around a hundred feet until you reach the ice. It shows clearly from the ravine floor and tends to form early in the season, so check the avalanche forecast.",
   "area_id": "nh_tuckerman_ravine",
   "descent": null,
   "descent_text": null,
   "description": null,
   "discipline": "ice",
   "grade": "WI3",
